---
// Unlisted internal page — walks Roze through Stripe's own business/identity
// verification so real payments can go live. Not linked from nav or any
// sitemap; noindex below keeps it out of search results. This site has no
// customer auth (see CLAUDE.md non-goals), so "secret" here means obscure +
// unlisted, not access-controlled — fine for a page with no real secrets on
// it (generic instructions, not an actual SSN/account number).
//
// Deliberately skips the shared Layout: that component's global styles/nav
// are built for on-brand site pages, and this is a one-off reference doc for
// a single reader, styled independently so it can't drift when the site
// theme changes.
export const prerender = true;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" />
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
  <title>Stripe Activation Guide</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Petrona:ital,wght@0,500;0,600;0,700;1,500&family=Work+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@500;600&display=swap">
  <style is:global>
    :root{
      --bg:#EDE9E1;
      --bg-elevated:#F9F7F3;
      --ink:#2A2724;
      --ink-muted:#6B655D;
      --accent:#3D5A73;
      --accent-ink:#20323F;
      --accent-soft:#D8E1E6;
      --sage:#4F7350;
      --sage-soft:#E1EADD;
      --ochre:#96631E;
      --ochre-soft:#F3E3C6;
      --border:#DCD5C8;
      --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(42,39,36,0.06), 0 4px 16px rgba(42,39,36,0.05);
    }
    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){
      :root:not([data-theme="light"]){
        --bg:#1E1C1A;
        --bg-elevated:#28251F;
        --ink:#EDE8E0;
        --ink-muted:#AFA89B;
        --accent:#8FB2CC;
        --accent-ink:#DCEAF3;
        --accent-soft:#2B3C46;
        --sage:#8FB489;
        --sage-soft:#26332A;
        --ochre:#D9A354;
        --ochre-soft:#3A2C18;
        --border:#3C3730;
        --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.3), 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);
      }
    }
    :root[data-theme="dark"]{
      --bg:#1E1C1A;
      --bg-elevated:#28251F;
      --ink:#EDE8E0;
      --ink-muted:#AFA89B;
      --accent:#8FB2CC;
      --accent-ink:#DCEAF3;
      --accent-soft:#2B3C46;
      --sage:#8FB489;
      --sage-soft:#26332A;
      --ochre:#D9A354;
      --ochre-soft:#3A2C18;
      --border:#3C3730;
      --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.3), 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);
    }

    *{box-sizing:border-box;}
    body{
      margin:0;
      background:var(--bg);
      color:var(--ink);
      font-family:"Work Sans", system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-size:17px;
      line-height:1.6;
      -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
    }
    .page{
      max-width:680px;
      margin:0 auto;
      padding:2.75rem 1.25rem 5rem;
    }
    h1,h2,h3{
      font-family:"Petrona", Georgia, serif;
      text-wrap:balance;
      margin:0;
      color:var(--ink);
    }
    p{ margin:0.6em 0; }
    a{ color:var(--accent); text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 45%, transparent); }
    a:focus-visible, button:focus-visible, summary:focus-visible{
      outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
      outline-offset: 3px;
    }

    /* ---------- Header ---------- */
    .masthead{
      display:flex;
      flex-direction:column;
      gap:0.9rem;
      padding-bottom:2rem;
      margin-bottom:2.25rem;
      border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .eyebrow{
      display:inline-flex;
      align-items:center;
      gap:0.5rem;
      font-family:"IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
      font-size:0.72rem;
      letter-spacing:0.14em;
      text-transform:uppercase;
      color:var(--accent-ink);
      background:var(--accent-soft);
      padding:0.35rem 0.7rem;
      border-radius:100px;
      width:fit-content;
    }
    .masthead h1{
      font-size:clamp(1.9rem, 6vw, 2.5rem);
      font-weight:700;
      line-height:1.15;
    }
    .masthead .dek{
      font-size:1.05rem;
      color:var(--ink-muted);
      max-width:52ch;
    }

    /* ---------- Intro note ---------- */
    .note{
      background:var(--bg-elevated);
      border:1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius:14px;
      padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;
      box-shadow:var(--shadow);
      margin:0 0 2.5rem;
    }
    .note p{ margin:0.5em 0; }
    .note p:first-child{ margin-top:0; }
    .note p:last-child{ margin-bottom:0; }

    /* ---------- Phase sections ---------- */
    .phase{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;
      gap:0 1.1rem;
      margin:2.75rem 0;
    }
    .stamp{
      grid-row: 1 / 3;
      width:2.9rem; height:2.9rem;
      border-radius:50%;
      background:var(--bg-elevated);
      border:1.5px solid var(--accent);
      color:var(--accent-ink);
      display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;
      font-family:"IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
      font-weight:600;
      font-size:1.1rem;
      box-shadow:var(--shadow);
    }
    .phase h2{
      font-size:1.35rem;
      font-weight:700;
      align-self:center;
      line-height:1.25;
    }
    .phase-label{
      font-family:"IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
      font-size:0.7rem;
      letter-spacing:0.12em;
      text-transform:uppercase;
      color:var(--ink-muted);
      grid-column:2;
      margin-bottom:0.15rem;
    }
    .phase-body{
      grid-column:2;
      margin-top:0.85rem;
    }
    .phase-body > p:first-child{ margin-top:0; }

    ul.steps, ul.gather{
      list-style:none;
      margin:0.9rem 0 0;
      padding:0;
      display:flex;
      flex-direction:column;
      gap:0.55rem;
    }
    ul.steps li, ul.gather li{
      position:relative;
      padding-left:1.7rem;
      background:var(--bg-elevated);
      border:1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius:10px;
      padding:0.65rem 0.9rem 0.65rem 2.1rem;
      box-shadow:var(--shadow);
    }
    ul.steps li::before{
      content:"";
      position:absolute;
      left:0.85rem; top:50%;
      transform:translateY(-50%);
      width:0.5rem; height:0.5rem;
      border-radius:50%;
      background:var(--accent);
    }
    ul.gather li::before{
      content:"✓";
      position:absolute;
      left:0.7rem; top:0.62rem;
      color:var(--sage);
      font-weight:700;
      font-size:0.85rem;
    }
    .steps strong, .gather strong{ color:var(--ink); }

    /* ---------- Skip callout ---------- */
    .skip{
      margin:1.1rem 0 0;
      background:var(--ochre-soft);
      border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ochre) 40%, var(--border));
      border-radius:14px;
      padding:1.1rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;
    }
    .skip-title{
      display:flex;
      align-items:center;
      gap:0.5rem;
      font-family:"IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
      font-size:0.78rem;
      letter-spacing:0.08em;
      text-transform:uppercase;
      color:var(--ochre);
      font-weight:600;
      margin-bottom:0.6rem;
    }
    .skip ul{
      margin:0;
      padding-left:0;
      list-style:none;
      display:flex;
      flex-direction:column;
      gap:0.4rem;
    }
    .skip li{
      padding-left:1.4rem;
      position:relative;
    }
    .skip li::before{
      content:"✕";
      position:absolute;
      left:0;
      color:var(--ochre);
      font-weight:700;
    }
    .skip .why{
      margin-top:0.75rem;
      font-size:0.92rem;
      color:var(--ink-muted);
    }

    /* ---------- Divider between big sections ---------- */
    .section-break{
      display:flex;
      align-items:center;
      gap:0.75rem;
      margin:3.25rem 0 0.5rem;
    }
    .section-break .stamp-lg{
      width:2.2rem;height:2.2rem;border-radius:50%;
      border:1.5px solid var(--sage);
      color:var(--sage);
      display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
      font-family:"IBM Plex Mono",monospace;
      font-weight:600; font-size:1rem;
      flex:none;
    }
    .section-break h2{ font-size:1.4rem; }

    /* ---------- Done box ---------- */
    .done{
      margin-top:1rem;
      background:var(--sage-soft);
      border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--sage) 40%, var(--border));
      border-radius:14px;
      padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;
    }
    .done p{ margin:0.4em 0; }

    /* ---------- FAQ ---------- */
    .faq{ margin-top:0.75rem; }
    details{
      background:var(--bg-elevated);
      border:1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius:10px;
      padding:0.75rem 1rem;
      margin-bottom:0.6rem;
      box-shadow:var(--shadow);
    }
    summary{
      cursor:pointer;
      font-weight:600;
      list-style:none;
      display:flex;
      justify-content:space-between;
      align-items:center;
      gap:0.75rem;
    }
    summary::-webkit-details-marker{ display:none; }
    summary::after{
      content:"+";
      font-family:"IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
      color:var(--accent);
      font-size:1.1rem;
      flex:none;
    }
    details[open] summary::after{ content:"–"; }
    details p{ margin:0.6rem 0 0.1rem; color:var(--ink-muted); }

    /* ---------- Footer ---------- */
    .footer{
      margin-top:3.5rem;
      padding-top:1.5rem;
      border-top:1px solid var(--border);
      color:var(--ink-muted);
      font-size:0.88rem;
    }

    code{
      font-family:"IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
      font-size:0.9em;
      background:var(--accent-soft);
      color:var(--accent-ink);
      padding:0.1em 0.4em;
      border-radius:5px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="page">

    <header class="masthead">
      <span class="eyebrow">🏺 myfriendroze · going live</span>
      <h1>Stripe Activation Guide</h1>
      <p class="dek">Roze — this is the last step before the website can take real payments. It's about 15 minutes of paperwork inside Stripe itself. Nothing here touches the website or needs a computer — your phone is fine.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="note">
      <p><strong>Where things stand:</strong> the checkout on myfriendroze.com is already built and tested — we ran a real practice purchase through it and it worked. The only thing left is that Stripe (the company that actually moves the money into your bank account) needs to verify who you are before it will handle real dollars. That's what the wizard on your phone is.</p>
      <p><strong>The confusing part:</strong> that same wizard also tries to walk you through building an entire online store inside Stripe — product pages, a checkout design, all of it. Skip every bit of that. We already have our own store. You only need the sections about <em>your business and your bank account</em>. Those are marked below.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section-break">
      <span class="stamp-lg">✓</span>
      <h2>Before you open the app</h2>
    </div>
    <p style="color:var(--ink-muted); margin-top:0.35rem;">Have these on hand first so you're not hunting for them mid-form. None of this needs to be exact to the penny — reasonable answers are fine.</p>

    <ul class="gather">
      <li><strong>Your legal name</strong>, and the business name if you use one. If myfriendroze isn't a registered LLC or corporation, that's fine — you'll select <strong>"sole proprietor" / "individual"</strong>, which just means the business is legally you.</li>
      <li><strong>Home or business address</strong> — a home address is completely normal for a shop this size.</li>
      <li><strong>Social Security Number</strong> (or an EIN, only if the business has one). This is standard for every payment processor, not specific to Stripe — see the FAQ below on why.</li>
      <li><strong>Date of birth.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>A photo ID</strong> — driver's license or passport. You'll photograph it with your phone camera during the identity step.</li>
      <li><strong>Bank account and routing number</strong> — wherever you want sale proceeds deposited.</li>
      <li><strong>A rough guess at monthly sales</strong> — "$500," "$1,000," whatever's realistic. It's an estimate, not a commitment.</li>
      <li><strong>The website address:</strong> <code>myfriendroze.com</code></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="section-break">
      <span class="stamp-lg">→</span>
      <h2>Finding the form</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="steps" style="margin-top:0.85rem;">
      <li>Open the Stripe app, or go to <code>dashboard.stripe.com</code> in a browser and log into the existing account.</li>
      <li>Look for a banner or button that says something like <strong>"Activate your account"</strong> or <strong>"Activate payments"</strong> — usually right on the home screen. If you don't see it, check <strong>Settings → Business settings</strong>.</li>
      <li>Tapping it starts the setup flow. It's broken into a few sections — walk through them in order, the app won't let you skip ahead anyway.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="phase">
      <div class="stamp">1</div>
      <div class="phase-label">Do this</div>
      <h2>Business details</h2>
      <div class="phase-body">
        <p>Asks what kind of business this is, what it sells, and where. Straightforward answers:</p>
        <ul class="steps">
          <li><strong>Business type:</strong> Individual / Sole proprietor, unless you've actually registered an LLC.</li>
          <li><strong>Industry:</strong> something like "Retail — Art, crafts, handmade goods."</li>
          <li><strong>Product description:</strong> "Handmade ceramics" is plenty.</li>
          <li><strong>Website:</strong> <code>myfriendroze.com</code></li>
          <li><strong>Statement descriptor:</strong> what shows up on a customer's card statement — "MYFRIENDROZE" works well.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="phase">
      <div class="stamp">2</div>
      <div class="phase-label">Do this</div>
      <h2>Verify your identity</h2>
      <div class="phase-body">
        <p>Your legal name, date of birth, SSN, and address, plus a photo of your ID taken right in the app. This is the part regulators require — it's confirming a real person is behind the account, same as opening a bank account.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="phase">
      <div class="stamp">3</div>
      <div class="phase-label">Do this</div>
      <h2>Add your payout bank account</h2>
      <div class="phase-body">
        <p>Account and routing number for where money should land. This is a standard linked-account step, not a purchase or a fee — Stripe is telling you where to <em>send</em> money, not taking any.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="phase">
      <div class="stamp">4</div>
      <div class="phase-label">Ignore this</div>
      <h2>Anything about building a store</h2>
      <div class="phase-body">
        <div class="skip">
          <div class="skip-title">Skip if you see it</div>
          <ul>
            <li>"Set up your online store" / "Create a storefront"</li>
            <li>"Add your first product" or any product catalog screen</li>
            <li>"Create a payment link"</li>
            <li>"Customize your checkout page" branding/theme editor</li>
            <li>"Connect a sales channel" (Shopify, social selling, etc.)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="why">Our website already builds the checkout page itself and sends Stripe the order directly — none of Stripe's own store-building tools are involved. If one of these pops up mid-flow, look for a "skip," "not now," or an X — it's never required to finish activation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-break">
      <span class="stamp-lg">✓</span>
      <h2>When you're done</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="done">
      <p>You'll know it worked when the dashboard stops nagging you to activate and shows something like <strong>"You're ready to accept live payments."</strong></p>
      <p>At that point, just let Emily know it's finished. There's a short step on the website side — swapping in the live keys Stripe just issued — that only needs to happen once, and it's not something you need to do. Nothing goes live on the site until that's done, so there's no rush or risk in between.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section-break">
      <span class="stamp-lg">?</span>
      <h2>Questions you'll probably have</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Why does it need my Social Security Number?</summary>
        <p>Every payment processor — Stripe, Square, PayPal, your bank — is legally required to verify who's on the other end of an account that moves money, to prevent fraud and money laundering. It's the same requirement as opening a business bank account, not something specific to us or unusually invasive.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is my information safe?</summary>
        <p>It goes directly to Stripe, not to us — myfriendroze's website and Firebase backend never see or store it. Stripe is the same payment processor used by Amazon, Shopify, and most major online retailers.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How long does verification take?</summary>
        <p>Often instant. Sometimes Stripe holds it for manual review, which can take a day or two — that's normal for a new account and not something to worry about.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What if it asks for more documents afterward?</summary>
        <p>Also normal — sometimes Stripe follows up asking for a clearer ID photo or a utility bill to confirm an address. Upload whatever's requested; it doesn't mean anything went wrong.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What if I get stuck or something looks wrong?</summary>
        <p>Stop and send Emily a screenshot rather than guessing — some fields (like the statement descriptor or business type) are easier to fix before submitting than after.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="footer">
      <p>That's the whole list. Everything else — the website, the checkout, the emails — is already built and waiting on just this.</p>
    </div>

  </div>
</body>
</html>
